  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the photoelectric equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p>Using this equation for the given two cases,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>280</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p>On subtracting,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1240</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>120</mn><mrow><mn>280</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1.3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8722;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
